[Ultracache](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache#ultracache) is supported on Nx 24.0.0 and later.
On those versions, CI runs use it by default once [Ultracache is on](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache#turn-on-ultracache) for your workspace in Nx Cloud.

[`NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE`](/docs/reference/environment-variables) changes the default for a run, and Nx 23 can opt in with it:

| Nx version       | In CI, unset | `NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE=true` | `NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE=false` |
| ---------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| 24.0.0 and later | On           | On                             | Off                             |
| 23.x             | Off          | On                             | Off                             |
| Before 23.0.0    | Off          | The run fails                  | Off                             |

Outside CI, every version hashes from declared `inputs` unless the run sets `NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE` to `true`.
If the workspace's Ultracache setting is off, every run hashes from declared `inputs`, whatever the variable says.

## Opt in on Nx 23

Set the variable in your CI environment:

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
env:
  NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE: 'true'
```

With the variable set to `true`, a run fails if Nx Cloud can't return the task's recording or a recording report is incomplete.
Without it, Nx makes one attempt to read the recordings, waits up to 10 seconds, and falls back to declared `inputs` if the read fails.

## Opt a run out

Set `NX_CLOUD_USE_ULTRACACHE` to `false` to hash every task in that run from its declared `inputs`.
To turn Ultracache off for a single target instead, set [`ultracache.mode`](/docs/reference/project-configuration#ultracache) to `off`.
